### Method D — Non-Jailbroken: Patch the IPA

When you only have the IPA and no JB device:

#### D.1 — Objection PatchIPA (easiest)

```bash
objection patchipa \
  --source Target.ipa \
  --codesign-signature <YOUR_CERT_HASH>
# Produces: Target-patched.ipa
# Sideload via Xcode, Sideloadly, or AltStore
# Then run Frida against the gadget
```

#### D.2 — Static Binary Patch (Hopper/Ghidra)

1. Open binary in Hopper or Ghidra
2. Find `SecTrustEvaluateWithError`
3. Replace prologue with: `MOV X0, #1 ; RET` (arm64) or `return 1`
4. For AFNetworking: NOP out `evaluateServerTrust:forDomain:` body, force `return true`
5. Resign: `ldid -S patched-binary && zip -r Target-patched.ipa app/`

#### D.3 — Load a Dylib (optool / insert_dylib)

```bash
# If patchipa fails, manually inject FridaGadget or libsubstitute
insert_dylib @executable_path/FridaGadget.dylib app/Payload/App.app/App
ldid -S app/Payload/App.app/App
zip -r Target-patched.ipa app/
```

**Resigning on Windows**: Use a macOS VM or CI (`codesign --force --sign <dev-id> --entitlements Entitlements.plist`).

**Alternative (TrollStore)**: Avoid resigning entirely on iOS 15.0–16.6.1 or 17.0 with TrollStore.

