### Method E — Plist Patching (ATS Pinning Only)

For apps using *only* iOS 14+ `NSPinnedDomains` in `Info.plist`:

```bash
unzip Target.ipa -d app/

# Edit app/Payload/App.app/Info.plist:
# Remove or empty the NSPinnedDomains section
```

**Before:**
```xml
<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
<dict>
    <key>NSPinnedDomains</key>
    <dict>
        <key>api.target.com</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPinnedCAIdentities</key>
            <array>
                <dict><key>SPKI-SHA256-BASE64</key><string>...</string></dict>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </dict>
</dict>
```

**After:**
```xml
<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
<dict>
    <key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoads</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
```

Then resign and sideload.

> **Note**: This only works if the app relies *solely* on ATS pinning. Most production apps layer a code-level check on top.

