## Phase 4 — Common Failure Modes & Quick Fixes

| Symptom | Likely Cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **App crashes on launch** | Jailbreak / Frida detection | C.7 hooks; or `frida --runtime=v8`; or rename `frida-server` binary |
| **`Failed to attach: unable to connect`** | `frida-server` not running or version mismatch | `pkill frida-server; frida-server &` on device; verify `frida --version` matches `frida-server --version` |
| **Burp shows no traffic, app shows no errors** | CA installed but not trusted for TLS | Settings → About → Certificate Trust Settings → enable for CA |
| **`NSURLErrorDomain -1200`** | TLS handshake fail — proxy CA missing OR pinning still on | Verify CA in Safari first; then re-check bypass |
| **Some requests proxied, others blocked** | App uses two HTTP stacks (NSURLSession + Alamofire) | Layer hooks: C.1 + C.4 + C.5 as needed |
| **Bypass works once, fails on re-launch** | App caches pin result in keychain / background re-pin | Hook `keychainServices` or rerun bypass with `--no-pause -f` each launch |
| **Flutter app — nothing works** | BoringSSL inside Flutter ignores system trust | C.5 path: must hit Flutter's `ssl_crypto_x509_session_verify_cert_chain` |
| **React Native / NativeScript** | JS-layer pinning via `react-native-ssl-pinning` npm package | Frida-hook the bridge call OR patch the JS bundle in the IPA |

